  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#PersonalInformation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Personal Information</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Information relating to an individual's identity, background, and biographical details. Induced from a Placed as subClassOf InsuredIndividual (Stage 5, confidence: high); cluster of 8 surface variant(s) merged in Stage 3…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy suspends upon relocation to sanctioned country. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence links relocation to a sanctioned country with policy suspension, and 'PolicySuspension' is the appropriate st…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Rating improves based on health metrics, affecting premium. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows health metric improvements lead to premium reductions, directly linking the personal information t…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Occupation change is restricted, affecting premium stability. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence indicates that occupation changes trigger premium adjustments, and the prohibition is tied to maintain…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Spouse receives payout under specified conditions. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies that proof of death triggers a benefit payout to the spouse, making 'Benefit' the correct outcome class…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Index participation ≠ stock ownership. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence explicitly states that index participation does not equate to stock ownership. The classes 'PersonalInformation' and 'Index'…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy actions require owner consent. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows that owner consent is mandatory for policy changes, particularly option switches. The property links the personal inform…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Benefit payments capped at 24 months. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence consistently states a 24-month limit on benefits, with the insured as the subject. The cardinality 24 aligns with the '24-Mont…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Conversion without medical proof. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms that conversion does not require evidence of insurability. The property links personal information to the eligibility con…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Liability is prohibited until notice is received. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies that liability is not incurred until formal notice is received, and the notice must be documented. This…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Disease coverage is limited to deployment periods. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms that disease coverage applies only during deployment, which is a time-bound condition. The property link…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Trust beneficiary receives proceeds upon default. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows that upon trust default, the beneficiary receives proceeds, linking the personal information to the conditio…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assignments preserve the insured's identity. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms that assignments do not change the insureds listed on the policy. The property reflects that the insured's ide…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy changes require eligibility conditions. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence describes conditions for switching options and amending policies. The property governs eligibility for policy changes…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policyholder entitled to survivor benefit upon survivorship. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence describes entitlement to a survivor benefit under survivorship conditions, and 'SurvivorshipLifeInsuran…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Personal information is disjoint from liability limitation. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The classes are unrelated: personal information pertains to identity, while liability limitation governs claim priori…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Higher policy overrides lower in conflicts. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows individuals are subject to policy hierarchy decisions. The property links personal data to policy contracts, justi…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Conversion requires ownership transfer documents. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms documents are required for conversion. The property links personal information to document submission, ju…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Withdrawals are tax-free if the policyholder is at least age 18. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies age 18 as the threshold for tax-free withdrawals, and AgeRange is the appropriate class f…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Proof of death is required for benefit payment. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence requires documentation of death for payout, and 'Document' is the correct range. The property links personal informa…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Re-underwriting is required for new or reinstated coverage. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows re-underwriting applies during reinstatement or new coverage, and the property links personal info…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policyholder must have insurable interest at issuance. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; Insurable interest is a condition tied to the policyholder's relationship with the insured, and the requirement applies to…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Health metric threshold for preferred insurance tier. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; Cholesterol levels are a health metric used in underwriting, and the threshold is a quantitative requirement. The range is…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policyholder must have documented family health history. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; Family health history is a documented medical requirement for eligibility, applied to individuals during underwriting. T…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Guaranteed issue up to coverage limit. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence links personal information (age) to a coverage limit. The property defines a limit, so someValuesFrom is appropriate; source…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Death from insurrection excluded. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows death from insurrection triggers an exclusion. The property links personal information to an exclusion, so someValuesFrom is…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Basic benefits depend on income brackets. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence clearly links income ranges (e.g., $30K–$40K) to specific benefit amounts ($50K), establishing a direct relationship betwe…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A subject is prohibited from accessing managed accounts. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The hierarchy shows no subclass relationship between PersonalInformation and Account, and they share no common subclass.…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Membership is required for coverage eligibility. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows that membership in NAIFA or a mutual society is required for coverage, linking personal status to coverage el…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Marital status change requires beneficiary update. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence indicates that a change in marital status may require updating the contingent beneficiary designation, linking pe…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">IED death coverage depends on age eligibility. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property applies to individuals and is tied to coverage eligibility, which is contextually linked to age ranges. The evidence…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Diving coverage eligibility after year 5 excludes prior restrictions. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows diving coverage is excluded in years 1–5 and becomes eligible after year 5. The property…</rdfs:comment>
