  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#DateWindow">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Date Window</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A time period defined by a start and end date, often specifying validity or eligibility duration. Induced from a Placed as subClassOf owl:Thing (Stage 5, confidence: high); cluster of 4 surface variant(s) merged in Stage…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Coverage eligibility must begin within a time window. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows that eligibility must begin within a defined window after a qualifying event, such as separation or poli…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Penalty applies based on duration of nondisclosure. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence links the penalty to the duration of undisclosed use, such as tobacco use. The property captures this temporal d…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Severance request must be submitted before deadline. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies a deadline for severance requests tied to policy expiry or first-to-die events, which are time-based…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Accidental death claims must be filed within a time window. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence consistently specifies time windows (e.g., 60, 90, 120, 180 days) for submitting accidental death claims…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policyholder must die before deadline to trigger benefit. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies that payout occurs only if death happens before a certain date, establishing a temporal eligibil…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A rider can only be elected during open enrollment. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence states that riders can be elected during open enrollment, indicating a temporal eligibility condition. The prope…</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A time period defined by a start and end date, often specifying validity or eligibility duration.</skos:definition>
