  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#Benefit">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Benefit</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A monetary amount paid under a life insurance policy upon the occurrence of a specified event. Induced from a Placed as subClassOf DeathBenefit (Stage 5, confidence: high); cluster of 1 surface variant(s) merged in Stage…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Death benefit eligibility depends on reinsured amount. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence indicates that death benefit eligibility is tied to the amount reinsured by co-insurers, particularly in case…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Maximum benefit amount is capped at two units. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence mentions 'Two-Year Gain Cap' and 'Two-Year Sum Cap', indicating a cardinality of two for capped benefit periods. The…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Terminal acceleration is capped at a maximum amount. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies a one-time acceleration and a maximum cap of $500,000, indicating a strict upper limit. This supports…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Excess benefits are subject to payout constraints. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The hierarchy shows Benefit and MonetaryAmount as unrelated classes with no shared subclasses. The evidence confirms excess be…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Terrorism benefit requires a rider to be in effect. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms that a terrorism benefit is only payable if the corresponding rider is active, establishing a necessary…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Benefits are reduced during early policy years. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence links benefit reduction to early policy years, and the property specifies the temporal condition under which the red…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Specifies time-limited benefit eligibility period. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property defines a time-limited eligibility period for graded benefits, with evidence showing it applies over specific pol…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Benefit ceases when threshold is met. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; Chronic benefits cease when the remaining death benefit falls below $50,000, defining a monetary threshold for cessation; source cluster: B…</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A monetary amount paid under a life insurance policy upon the occurrence of a specified event.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#DeathBenefit"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ncb598afe76e6469cba597494ddb7b313b32"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ncb598afe76e6469cba597494ddb7b313b65"/>
