  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#PolicyContract">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Policy Contract</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A legally binding agreement outlining terms, conditions, and provisions of a life insurance policy. Induced from a Placed as subClassOf InsuranceContract (Stage 5, confidence: high); cluster of 43 surface variant(s) merg…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Maximum two waiver events allowed per policy. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence explicitly states a maximum of two waiver events per policy. The property is correctly mapped to the domain and range…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Riders are part of the entire insurance contract. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms that riders are components of the entire contract. The property is appropriately used to express that a p…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Contestability applies within a defined time period. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows that contestability is limited to a specific period after policy issuance. The property is correctly link…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Death proceeds may be excluded under certain conditions. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence indicates that death proceeds are subject to exclusion under specific conditions, such as IRS rules or buy-…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Coverage remains active during the grace period. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms that coverage continues during the grace period despite late payment. The property is appropriately used t…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy qualifies for estate tax exclusion via trust. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows that estate exclusion eligibility depends on trust structure and intent, which are defined by exclusion c…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Condition for coverage to begin. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows coverage begins only after meeting conditions like premium payment and enrollment. The activation condition is tied to the po…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Death must occur while policy is in force. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence requires the policy to be in force at the time of death for benefits to be payable. The property 'mustRemainAtOrBelowPerc…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Payouts across tranches within 30 days. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence states both tranches are paid within 30 days, indicating a maximum of 30 days for payout structure. The cardinality reflects…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A policy maintains coverage continuity when a conversion right is exercised. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows coverage continues after conversion, indicating a relationship between policy con…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Face amount must not exceed $1,000,000. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies a maximum face amount of $1,000,000, and the cardinality is inferred from the explicit limit in the sentence; sour…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">COI rates are fixed per a predefined schedule. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms COI rates are guaranteed not to exceed specified limits via a schedule, linking PolicyContract to Rate throu…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Survival order determines beneficiary payout eligibility. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies that survival order is contractually defined and governs payout distribution, making Contractual…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy splits into two upon severance. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence describes a policy splitting into two individual policies upon severance, directly linking PolicyContract to PolicySplit via…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Payouts are prohibited if insured is sanctioned. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms payouts are blocked if payment violates OFAC or other sanctions, establishing a clear link from PolicyCont…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A loan reduces the death benefit amount payable upon policyholder's death. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; Evidence confirms loans reduce death benefits dollar-for-dollar. The property links policy contracts t…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy contract defines complete agreement between parties. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The policy document constitutes the entire agreement, and the clause applies to contractual completeness. EntityDisso…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policyholder must meet conditions to retain non-forfeiture benefits. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; Evidence shows non-forfeiture options are available after three years of premium payments, and the policyhol…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy includes MSCI World minimum guarantee. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies a minimum guarantee tied to the MSCI World index, which is quantified as a percentage. This supports a someV…</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A legally binding agreement outlining terms, conditions, and provisions of a life insurance policy.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#InsuranceContract"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ncb598afe76e6469cba597494ddb7b313b24"/>
