    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Life Insurance Policy</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The root concept of this ontology. Represents a life insurance policy as a whole; all domain classes are subsumed under this concept.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Conversion is prohibited after a policy has already been converted. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence indicates that conversion is not allowed after an initial conversion, and the property reflects…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy cannot be transferred after termination. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; Evidence states that transfer is only allowed upon termination with specific conditions, implying eligibility is restricted post-…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A payment made at policy end under specific conditions. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows end-of-term payouts are benefits tied to policy maturity, with specific amounts paid upon survival. Th…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Death benefit paid as a single lump sum. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The sentences confirm the death benefit is paid in a lump sum, directly linking the policy to a monetary payout. The edge topology suppo…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A shadow account must be logically distinct from the primary policy account. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The hierarchy shows no subclass relationship between LifeInsurancePolicy and ShadowAccount, and they…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Benefits continue after premium exhaustion under conditions. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows benefits continue post-premium exhaustion with duration measured in years. The property is a cond…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">COI calculated using a specific formula. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The sentences describe COI as computed via mathematical expressions involving Net Amount at Risk and COI Rate. This matches the range 'C…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Self-injury claims are prohibited under the policy. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property defines a policy-level exclusion for self-injury. The classes 'LifeInsurancePolicy' and 'Exclusion' are disjoint…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy excludes guarantee on investment performance. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The hierarchy shows LifeInsurancePolicy and Portfolio as unrelated; no shared subclasses exist. The property explicitly deni…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inflation credit is prohibited upon policy termination. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property specifies that inflation credit is not payable upon termination, effectively excluding it from benefit payou…</rdfs:comment>
