    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Intended Yearly Contribution</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A periodic payment made to maintain insurance coverage, typically annual. Induced from a Hierarchy placement via graph-native parent (entity role co-occurrence): subClassOf FINANCIAL_INSTRUMENT; cluster of 7 surface vari…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Specifies when premium adjustments may occur. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows adjustments occur at policy anniversaries or prospectively after approval, indicating a temporal constraint. The…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Unpaid premiums must be retained until recovery or settlement. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence indicates unpaid premiums are retained until repayment or recovery, aligning with the property's doma…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Premiums are accepted under policy conditions. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The insurer accepts premiums under defined conditions, such as evidence of insurability. The property links Premium to LifeInsuran…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Premiums are recalculated when charity status changes. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows that changing from a charitable to non-charitable beneficiary triggers a recalibration to a standard mo…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Sets maximum flexible payment amount. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; Evidence specifies a $100 minimum per payment, indicating a cardinality constraint on the number of allowable payments. The filler is Monet…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Specifies premium load application or deduction. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property governs the percentage load applied to premiums, with evidence showing values like 3.0% and 5.50%. xsd:decimal is t…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A policy requires a premium exceeding 500 for jump-related coverage. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies that a premium over 500 triggers additional requirements for jump-related coverage. T…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">GPT enables higher premium flexibility. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence links GPT to increased premium flexibility, with adjustments tied to financial amounts. 'MonetaryAmount' is the appropriate…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A policy must return the premium plus interest that compounds annually. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property involves the return of premiums with compounded interest, which is a numerical value. The ev…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Triggers due diligence above threshold. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies a $50,000 annual premium threshold, indicating a condition that triggers enhanced due diligence, supported by a de…</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A periodic payment made to maintain insurance coverage, typically annual.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#RecurringPayment"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ncb598afe76e6469cba597494ddb7b313b2"/>
