  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#PersonalBenefitFloor">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Personal Benefit Floor</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A minimum level of personal benefit guaranteed in a life insurance policy. Induced from a Placed as subClassOf BenefitFramework (Stage 5, confidence: high); cluster of 1 surface variant(s) merged in Stage 3.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Ownership transfers upon reaching age threshold. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; Evidence shows ownership transfers at age 18 or 25. The property links a benefit floor to age-based transfer triggers; source cl…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Buy-sell agreement must be filed for policy eligibility. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; Evidence shows filing is required for binding agreements. The property links a benefit floor to rate-related contractual…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Fracture surgery triggers a benefit payout. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The sentences confirm a lump-sum indemnity is payable for fracture surgery, establishing a direct link between the event and a benefi…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Ownership transfers under predefined conditions like death or dissolution. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The domain 'PersonalBenefitFloor' is linked to ownership transfer events involving policy transfer, an…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Premiums are continued during specified types of leave. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows premiums continue during FMLA and medical leave, with financial obligations tied to the leave event; s…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Spouse substitution requires a specified age range. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies an age range (45–80) for spouse substitution, directly linking the eligibility condition to an AgeRang…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Personal benefit floor includes burn qualification benefits. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows that burns qualify for a specific benefit, and the personal benefit floor is tied to injury-based…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policyholder must be below age limit for port coverage. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property defines an age threshold for eligibility in portability coverage. The range 'AgeRange' appropriately capture…</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A minimum level of personal benefit guaranteed in a life insurance policy.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#BenefitFramework"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ncb598afe76e6469cba597494ddb7b313b90"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ncb598afe76e6469cba597494ddb7b313b92"/>
