  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#InsuredPerson">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">First Insured Under Policy</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A person who is insured under a life insurance policy, regardless of order or designation. Induced from a Hierarchy placement via graph-native parent (entity role co-occurrence): subClassOf PERSON; cluster of 28 surface…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Premiums are recalculated based on the policyholder's attained age. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; Premiums are recalculated based on attained age, a core underwriting mechanism. The property links insured in…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A requirement that medical verification must be performed by the insurer. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The insurer has the right to require medical verification, which applies to insured individuals. The pr…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Benefit payable for loss of both hands or feet. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms that loss of both hands or feet triggers a full AD&amp;D benefit payout. The property links the insured person…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Adjusts benefits for misstated age or sex at inception. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property governs benefit adjustments due to misstated personal data, and 'Benefit' is the correct range. The evidence…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Ordained minister status required for eligibility. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence states ordained status is required for eligibility, establishing a direct relationship between the person and the…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Personal benefits are prohibited under self-dealing rules. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence prohibits personal benefits tied to pledges and encumbrances, and the property aligns with the restrictio…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policyholders must report avocation changes. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence indicates that insured persons have an ongoing obligation to report changes in avocations, which are specific activitie…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Contractors are excluded from eligibility. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The hierarchy shows InsuredPerson and Occupation as unrelated with no shared subclasses. The evidence confirms contractors (a type of…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Seat belt usage qualifies for bonus benefit. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows that wearing a seat belt triggers an additional death benefit, linking the insured person to the benefit via the…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A condition that activates a policy provision when cognitive impairment is present. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows cognitive impairment triggers policy provisions and is certified by licens…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A person with a hazardous occupation is excluded from coverage. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The class 'InsuredPerson' and 'Exclusion' are disjoint: a person cannot be both an insured and an exclusion. No s…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Conversion triggers loss of inflation credit. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property describes a loss of inflation credit upon conversion, with domain 'InsuredPerson' and range 'Credit'. Evidence confirm…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Insured must act within official duties. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence states that an act qualifies as 'Line of Duty' only when ordered by a superior officer, indicating a condition-based eligib…</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A person who is insured under a life insurance policy, regardless of order or designation.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#InsuredPersonOrEntity"/>
