    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Beneficiaries must provide verified identity documents. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence requires proof of identity and relationship for claims. The property mandates submission of verified documen…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Hierarchical priority for benefit distribution among relatives. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The classes are disjoint: beneficiaries are persons, while distribution initiation is a procedural state. They sh…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Beneficiary payout shares are proportionally allocated. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property governs payout shares among beneficiaries, with evidence showing exact percentage allocations. 'PercentageAl…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Non-US beneficiaries face withholding tax. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms that non-US beneficiaries are subject to withholding tax, which is a binary condition. The property is appropria…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Beneficiary and distribution method are disjoint. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows that per stirpes distribution is a rule governing how benefits are allocated, not a type of beneficiary. The…</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A person or entity designated to receive death benefit proceeds from a life insurance policy.</skos:definition>
