    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Account</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A financial account within a life insurance policy holding policy values and subject to specified terms. Induced from a Placed as subClassOf InvestmentVehicle (Stage 5, confidence: high); cluster of 5 surface variant(s)…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Interest rates are determined by tiered thresholds with caps, floors, and rate bands. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows account value tiers determine different interest rates, with specific ca…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy must maintain minimum balance after transactions. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property governs minimum balance thresholds, which are financial amounts. Evidence confirms such thresholds exist, m…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Embedded fees reduce index account performance. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows embedded fees in proprietary index accounts reduce gross performance. The property is a direct link from an ac…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Specifies method for two-year sum credit calculation. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property defines a financial formula applied to an account for two-year sum credit. Evidence confirms it governs credit…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Credits are prohibited before account maturity. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence states no crediting occurs before maturity, implying a strict exclusion. The classes are disjoint as accounts and cr…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Company absorbs loss up to a threshold. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies that the company absorbs losses up to a defined percentage, which is a monetary threshold applied to the account;…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A rate increase is triggered when a threshold is exceeded. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property links an account to a rate increase condition. The evidence shows that exceeding a threshold triggers a r…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Pending credits remain active after policyholder's death. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence states pending credits remain in effect after death, and the edge topology confirms Account relates to Cre…</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A financial account within a life insurance policy holding policy values and subject to specified terms.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#InvestmentVehicle"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ncb598afe76e6469cba597494ddb7b313b99"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ncb598afe76e6469cba597494ddb7b313b178"/>
